@71009 = ~exalted fighter~
@71 = ~Exalted Fighter~
@72 = ~EXALTED FIGHTER: Some warriors live only to fight, swear by war, and dream of nothing but victory. The most fanatical seek every possible source of power to crush their foes.
If such a fighter discovers an innate gift for magic, he may see it as another source of strength and choose to learn how to wield it. In doing so, he becomes a warlord.

Advantages:
- No special advantages until he becomes a mage.
- To dual-class into a mage, he needs only 17 Intelligence and 12 Wisdom; his physical ability scores do not matter.

Disadvantages:
- Considers only true weapons of war worthy of study.
- His obsession with power prevents him from being lawful good.
- Regards ranged combat as cowardly and refuses to use missile weapons.~

@7309 = ~warlord~
@73 = ~Warlord~
@74 = ~WARLORD: A warlord is a fanatical fighter who sees his innate arcane gift as a way to become a merciless engine of war. While continuing his martial training, he focuses his magical discoveries on what he considers essential: becoming stronger in battle and devastating enemy ranks. Ignoring traditional magic, he develops his own repertoire of spells, all intended for combat.
A proud warrior, he shuns "cowardly" tactics such as sheltering behind summoned creatures or fighting from a distance. He has no interest in honorable combat, however, and will inflict the worst torments on his foes, from mental ruin to utter annihilation.

Advantages:
- Because magic comes to him instinctively, he can continue his martial training, retaining some of his fighting abilities:
  * Gains 1 additional hit point per level.
  * Gains a +1 bonus to his saving throw vs. death every 4 levels, up to +5.
  * Uses the cleric THAC0 progression.
  * May cast spells in any armor once he has regained his fighter abilities.
- Reflection during moments of respite allows him to discover new spells regularly.
- His spell memorization capacity grows faster than that of a conventional mage.

Disadvantages:
- His magic is innate; he does not understand arcane theory and can neither use magical scrolls nor learn spells from them.
- Time spent on martial training slows his progress as a mage (-15% experience).
- Regards ranged combat as cowardly and refuses to use missile weapons.~

